Convert to Memory Initialization:

# Convert binary to Verilog memory format
python3 -c "
import sys
with open('build_output/snake.bin', 'rb') as f:
    data = f.read()
with open('firmware.hex', 'w') as f:
    for i, byte in enumerate(data):
        f.write(f'{byte:02x}\n')
        if i % 4 == 3: f.write('\n')
"

Implementation Flow
Simulate → iverilog + vvp (Verify logic works)

Synthesize → yosys (Convert to gates)

Place & Route → nextpnr (Map to FPGA)

Generate Bitstream → icepack (Create .bin file)

Program FPGA → iceprog (Load onto board)

 Key Insights:
C code alone doesn't run on FPGA - needs hardware infrastructure

Memory addresses in C must match hardware implementation

Always simulate before deploying to FPGA

Your game logic is good - just needs proper hardware support

Build command
